            <ArticleTitle>Monocytes in acute coronary syndromes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1433-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1161/ATVBAHA.108.180513</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of this overview is to summarize the available data on the involvement of monocytes in the pathological processes related to the development of acute coronary syndromes and the recovery of damaged areas, the prevention of excessive inflammatory and procoagulant response, and the restoration of microcirculation (angiogenesis).</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
